WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.651
A coding agent is a model that uses tools in a loop.

00:00:04.001 --> 00:00:06.646
It isn't autocomplete, and it isn't a chatbot.

00:00:06.996 --> 00:00:09.641
It reads files, runs commands and edits code,

00:00:09.641 --> 00:00:12.756
from a terminal, an editor, a desktop app or the web.

00:00:13.106 --> 00:00:15.292
It picks which tools to use from your prompt,

00:00:15.292 --> 00:00:17.138
and from what it learns along the way.

00:00:18.538 --> 00:00:21.034
Give it a task, and it works in three phases.

00:00:21.384 --> 00:00:24.805
It gathers context, takes action, then verifies the result,

00:00:24.805 --> 00:00:27.357
and goes round again until the task is done.

00:00:27.707 --> 00:00:29.302
You can step in at any point.

00:00:29.302 --> 00:00:32.657
Press Escape to stop it, or type a correction and it adjusts.

00:00:33.007 --> 00:00:35.396
Risky actions are checked before they run:

00:00:35.396 --> 00:00:39.151
in manual mode it asks you, in auto mode a classifier blocks them.

00:00:40.551 --> 00:00:43.879
Before you type a word, its context window is already filling.

00:00:44.229 --> 00:00:47.654
System instructions. Your CLAUDE.md. Saved memory.

00:00:47.654 --> 00:00:52.037
A short description of every skill. The names of your MCP tools.

00:00:52.387 --> 00:00:55.565
Then your prompt, and everything it reads and runs after that.

00:00:55.915 --> 00:00:59.289
When the window gets full, old tool output is cleared first,

00:00:59.289 --> 00:01:01.313
then the conversation is summarized.

00:01:02.713 --> 00:01:06.980
So context is a budget, and every layer in this series spends some of it.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:10.371
Slash context shows what loaded, and what each part costs.

00:01:10.721 --> 00:01:14.266
Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI and Copilot run the same loop,

00:01:14.266 --> 00:01:16.481
with their own names for the parts.

00:01:16.831 --> 00:01:18.560
Everyone rents the same models.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:21.013
The setup around them is the part you build.
